      {
        "title": "Show HN: demake – one source project compiles to any retro game console ROM",
        "link": "https://geosona.com/demake/",
        "description": "<p>This started life as a graphics tool for a specific problem: gen AI can make retro-styled sprites but can't follow exact hardware constraints of pixels and colors.<p>While building this I liked the idea that I can fan-out to any retro videogame console or handheld's specifications.<p>I then devised my own declarative language - Demotic - to express the game you want to build as concisely and naturally as possible without implementation detail. To work on different machines, you use relative units, like vw, vh, vmin, vmax.<p>It has a web UI, CLI and NPM package. Still a work in progress.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49195251\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49195251</a></p>\n<p>Points: 17</p>\n<p># Comments: 2</p>",
        "pubDate": "Thu, 06 Aug 2026 11:28:00 +0000",
